Two things still unchanged from the previous run
The Wildcard DNS curl commands are still scheme-less. The two Wildcard DNS replay commands are still:
curl -i -sS '3BbW9p14UnI5YWxkqrvGOC0S5ns-...nummus.robinhood.com'
curl -i -sS '3BbW9p14UnI5YWxkqrvGOC0S5ns-...api.robinhood.com'
Phase 3 of the fix plan (URL normalization in reproduction.py) hasn't landed yet. These E2E replay commands are generated by the test harness from finding metadata, not by the reporter — so the reporter-side fix won't change these. The E2E harness itself needs to apply _canonicalize_url before writing replay commands to the trace JSON. This is a separate touch point from the reporter fix.
File sizes are identical to the previous run — PDF is 12,997 bytes, DOCX is 38,715 bytes, same generated_at timestamps from March 29. The report was not regenerated from scratch; the reporter returned the already-completed artifact from the existing row. This is correct behavior — create_or_reset_report with the same scan_id and format returns the existing completed report ID, and generation is skipped because it's already completed. If you want to verify the Phase 1 description fixes actually appear in the report content, you need to either delete the existing report rows and regenerate, or use a different scan as the findings source.
The one structural note
The scan 7ee68848 has now appeared as status: running in two consecutive runs — the April 5 run and this April 6 run — with started_at: 2026-04-05T12:57:45. That scan has been running for over 12 hours. The watchdog in core_engine/watchdog.py should have marked it failed_internal after 2 hours. Either the watchdog isn't firing, the scan has somehow completed and the E2E is reading stale data, or the scan row is in a state the watchdog doesn't catch. Worth checking directly:
sqlSELECT scan_id, status, started_at, completed_at, error_detail 
FROM scans 
WHERE scan_id = '7ee68848-8ba3-4fb6-ab50-24256e2255eb';
If it's still running after 12+ hours that's a watchdog bug, not an E2E issue — but it should be diagnosed before it accumulates more stuck scans.
Summary
The plan's Phase 4 changes are correctly implemented. Phase 3 (URL normalization) is not yet reflected in the E2E replay commands, and the report content fixes from Phase 1 can't be verified without forcing a fresh report generation. The passed_with_fallback outcome label, environment-conditional download proof, and scan_source_outcome tracing are all working exactly as designed.